{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויכפר", :translit "vayechaper", :gloss "and he atoned"} {:he "לכפר", :translit "lechaper", :gloss "to atone"} {:he "ויכפר", :translit "vayechaper", :gloss "and he atoned"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Form ויכפר (vav-conversive perfect) denotes ongoing completed action rather than לכפר (infinitive), indicating continuous atonement."}], :frame {:text "Phinehas's zealous act is rewarded with a covenant of peace and eternal priesthood (Numbers 25:12-13). His act of zealotry is identified as the same zeal that Abraham displayed when he pursued the kings (Genesis 14:15), establishing a paradigm of righteous zeal. The Talmud links Phinehas to Elijah, stating that Phinehas is Elijah (Yerushalmi Nedarim 3:8), an immortal figure who stands and serves as an advocate for Israel in every generation.", :sources ["Numbers 25:12-13" "Genesis 14:15" "Yerushalmi Nedarim 3:8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Form ויכפר (vav-conversive perfect) denotes ongoing completed action rather than לכפר (infinitive), indicating continuous atonement.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:30.772330594Z", :model "glm-5.2"}